---
import ThemeInit from '../../components/ThemeInit.astro';
import '../../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="How Meridian Mobility unified a fragmented vehicle marketplace into one clear, responsive experience." />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>Meridian Mobility Case Study — Avery Rowan</title>
    <ThemeInit />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#case-study">Skip to case study</a>

    <header class="case-nav container">
      <a class="case-brand" href="/" aria-label="Back to Avery Rowan home">
        <strong>Avery</strong>
        <span>Designer and Creator</span>
      </a>
      <a class="back-link" href="/#works">← Back to work</a>
      <button class="icon-button theme-toggle case-theme" type="button" aria-label="Use dark mode" aria-pressed="false">
        <svg class="moon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20.4 15.2A8.4 8.4 0 0 1 8.8 3.6 8.5 8.5 0 1 0 20.4 15.2Z"/></svg>
        <svg class="sun" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><path d="M12 2v2M12 20v2M4.9 4.9l1.4 1.4M17.7 17.7l1.4 1.4M2 12h2M20 12h2M4.9 19.1l1.4-1.4M17.7 6.3l1.4-1.4"/></svg>
      </button>
    </header>

    <main class="case-main container" id="case-study">
      <article>
        <header class="case-header">
          <p class="case-kicker">Case study · Product design</p>
          <h1>Harmonize the Web Experience</h1>
          <p class="case-intro">Meridian Mobility had grown into three useful products that felt like three different companies. I helped the team turn them into one coherent marketplace without slowing down the people who relied on it every day.</p>
        </header>

        <figure class="case-hero">
          <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551650975-87deedd944c3?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1400&q=88" alt="Mobile marketplace screens used during the Meridian Mobility redesign" />
          <figcaption>A shared visual language across search, listings, and account tools.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <dl class="case-details">
          <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Product strategy, interaction and visual design</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Team</dt><dd>1 product manager, 4 engineers, 1 researcher</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Timeline</dt><dd>12 weeks in 2025</dd></div>
        </dl>

        <div class="case-body">
          <section>
            <p class="section-label">The challenge</p>
            <h2>Useful products, disconnected journeys</h2>
            <p>People could research a vehicle, compare local listings, and contact a seller, but each step used different navigation, filters, and terminology. Mobile visitors regularly lost their place when moving between sections, and support requests showed that account tools were especially difficult to find.</p>
            <p>The brief was not to redesign everything. It was to identify the smallest shared system that could make the entire journey feel dependable.</p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <p class="section-label">The approach</p>
            <h2>Follow the decisions people make</h2>
            <p>We interviewed recent buyers and sellers, reviewed search analytics, and mapped the questions people asked from first visit to final enquiry. That work shifted the project away from separate page templates and toward four recurring decisions: what to search, what to compare, whom to trust, and what to do next.</p>
            <blockquote>Consistency became a product feature, not simply a visual cleanup.</blockquote>
            <p>I prototyped the highest-traffic journey first, tested it at narrow screen widths, and worked with engineering to turn successful patterns into reusable components.</p>
          </section>

          <figure class="case-inline-image">
            <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1558655146-9f40138edfeb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1400&q=88" alt="Designer reviewing interface layouts and reusable components" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Testing the system across realistic content and screen sizes.</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <section>
            <p class="section-label">The solution</p>
            <h2>One system with room for context</h2>
            <p>A persistent search model, shared filter language, and predictable page hierarchy connected the marketplace. Listing cards adopted one information order, while contextual actions stayed flexible enough for cars, rentals, and property.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>A responsive navigation model shared across every product area</li>
              <li>Reusable search, filter, listing, and empty-state components</li>
              <li>Clearer saved-item and enquiry states for returning visitors</li>
              <li>Accessible focus, contrast, and reduced-motion behavior by default</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section>
            <p class="section-label">The outcome</p>
            <h2>A faster path from browsing to action</h2>
            <p>After launch, moderated testing showed fewer navigation errors and stronger confidence at every handoff. The shared component library also gave the product teams a common starting point for new work.</p>
            <div class="outcomes" aria-label="Project outcomes">
              <div><strong>28%</strong><span>faster listing completion</span></div>
              <div><strong>19%</strong><span>fewer navigation support requests</span></div>
              <div><strong>+11</strong><span>points in task confidence</span></div>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>

        <footer class="case-footer">
          <p>Next project</p>
          <a class="button secondary pill" href="/#works">Return to selected work</a>
        </footer>
      </article>
    </main>

    <script>
      const root = document.documentElement;
      const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.case-theme');

      function updateThemeButton() {
        const dark = root.dataset.theme === 'dark';
        if (button) {
          button.setAttribute('aria-label', dark ? 'Use light mode' : 'Use dark mode');
          button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(dark));
        }
      }

      button?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        root.dataset.theme = root.dataset.theme === 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark';
        localStorage.setItem('theme', root.dataset.theme);
        updateThemeButton();
      });
      updateThemeButton();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .case-nav { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto auto; align-items: center; gap: 24px; min-height: 176px; }
  .case-brand { display: inline-flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; width: max-content; gap: 3px; }
  .case-brand strong { font-size: 34px; line-height: 40px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.05em; }
  .case-brand span { color: var(--secondary); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4; }
  .back-link { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; }
  .back-link:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .case-main { padding-top: 72px; }
  .case-header { padding-bottom: 64px; }
  .case-kicker, .section-label { margin: 0 0 20px; color: var(--accent); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 1.5px; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .case-header h1 { max-width: 600px; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(42px, 7vw, 64px); line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -.045em; }
  .case-intro { margin: 28px 0 0; color: var(--secondary); font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .case-hero, .case-inline-image { margin: 0; }
  .case-hero img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; object-fit: cover; }
  .case-hero figcaption, .case-inline-image figcaption { margin-top: 10px; color: var(--tertiary); font-size: 13px; text-align: center; }
  .case-details { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; margin: 64px 0 0; padding: 32px 0; border-block: 1px solid var(--divider); }
  .case-details div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; }
  .case-details dt { color: var(--tertiary); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .case-details dd { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .case-body section { margin-top: 88px; }
  .case-body h2 { margin: 0 0 20px; font-size: 30px; line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .case-body p:not(.section-label), .case-body li { color: var(--secondary); }
  .case-body p:not(.section-label) { margin: 0; }
  .case-body p:not(.section-label) + p { margin-top: 20px; }
  .case-body blockquote { margin: 48px 0; padding-left: 24px; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.5; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .case-body ul { padding-left: 24px; }
  .case-body li + li { margin-top: 8px; }
  .case-inline-image { margin-top: 88px; }
  .case-inline-image img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16 / 10; object-fit: cover; }
  .outcomes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 40px; }
  .outcomes div { padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--divider); }
  .outcomes strong, .outcomes span { display: block; }
  .outcomes strong { color: var(--accent); font-size: 30px; line-height: 1.2; }
  .outcomes span { margin-top: 8px; color: var(--secondary); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .case-footer { margin-top: 96px; padding: 56px 0 80px; border-top: 1px solid var(--divider); }
  .case-footer p { margin: 0 0 20px; color: var(--secondary); }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .case-nav { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; min-height: 128px; gap: 16px; }
    .case-brand strong { font-size: 31px; line-height: 36px; }
    .back-link { display: none; }
    .case-main { padding-top: 48px; }
    .case-header { padding-bottom: 48px; }
    .case-header h1 { font-size: 42px; }
    .case-intro { font-size: 19px; }
    .case-details, .outcomes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .case-details { gap: 24px; }
    .case-body section, .case-inline-image { margin-top: 64px; }
  }
</style>
